{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-41338","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67057","text":"Handoff — A.3 closure commit, Relation Identity Kernel 0.1.2"}]},{"id":"blk-41339","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67058","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: all eight items of your commit ruling are landed, the battery is green at 782/782, and both pinned `sem-` ids are unmoved. Path A is ready to commit."}]},{"id":"blk-41340","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67059","text":"This memo replaces the 0.1.1 handoff. It is organised as your ruling was: one section per commit item, each stating what was wrong, what the repair is, and which check would catch a regression. Section 9 is the part that needs you — Path B, and two things I decided that I would rather you overturn now than later."}]},{"id":"blk-41341","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67060","text":"The verdict first"}]},{"id":"blk-41342","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"node test/conformance.mjs\n  782 passed, 0 failed  (70 annotated doc blocks of 113 swept, 26/26 capabilities cited)"},{"id":"blk-41343","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67061","text":"Pinned ids, re-verified live in the browser after every edit:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-41345","spans":[{"id":"spn-67062","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-41346","spans":[{"id":"spn-67063","text":""}]}],"id":"blk-41344","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-41347","spans":[{"id":"spn-67064","text":"starter world"}]},{"id":"blk-41348","spans":[{"id":"spn-67065","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-67e954cfe3115166b49388366df3f062a46572ba2baf53380f1520f4050b60ae"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41349","spans":[{"id":"spn-67066","text":"pinned fixture"}]},{"id":"blk-41350","spans":[{"id":"spn-67067","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-8ae91fe9cbc5fd086ce4356d587c403211e5c7b2b3ebdd316496367429ecfe4a"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-41351","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67068","text":"Neither moved. That is not incidental to this commit — items 1, 2 and 3 all change what the adapter "},{"id":"spn-67069","marks":["italic"],"text":"produces"},{"id":"spn-67070","text":", and if any of them had leaked into the spine's preimage those two lines would be different. The suite asserts byte equality between "},{"id":"spn-67071","marks":["code"],"text":"sealWithRelations"},{"id":"spn-67072","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-67073","marks":["code"],"text":"sealWorld"},{"id":"spn-67074","text":" for both fixtures before it runs anything else, so a leak fails loudly and first."}]},{"id":"blk-41352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67075","marks":["code"],"text":"rev-"},{"id":"spn-67076","text":" ids "},{"id":"spn-67077","marks":["bold"],"text":"did"},{"id":"spn-67078","text":" move, as expected and as designed: a revision now carries "},{"id":"spn-67079","marks":["code"],"text":"domain: \"signal\""},{"id":"spn-67080","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-67081","marks":["code"],"text":"texture: \"solid\""},{"id":"spn-67082","text":" where it previously carried "},{"id":"spn-67083","marks":["code"],"text":"domain: \"forge.world.core.v1\""},{"id":"spn-67084","text":" and no texture key. "},{"id":"spn-67085","marks":["code"],"text":"rev-"},{"id":"spn-67086","text":" is unpinned and world-independent by §D8.3; nothing published depends on its value."}]},{"id":"blk-41353","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67087","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-67088","marks":["code"],"text":"domain = signal"}]},{"id":"blk-41354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67089","marks":["bold"],"text":"Was."},{"id":"spn-67090","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67091","marks":["code"],"text":"edgeToRelationRevision"},{"id":"spn-67092","text":" wrote "},{"id":"spn-67093","marks":["code"],"text":"artifact.profile_id"},{"id":"spn-67094","text":" — the string "},{"id":"spn-67095","marks":["code"],"text":"forge.world.core.v1"},{"id":"spn-67096","text":" — into the "},{"id":"spn-67097","marks":["code"],"text":"domain"},{"id":"spn-67098","text":" slot."}]},{"id":"blk-41355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67099","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is wrong."},{"id":"spn-67100","text":" §D8's field table says a domain is a "},{"id":"spn-67101","marks":["italic"],"text":"profile-declared namespace"},{"id":"spn-67102","text":": "},{"id":"spn-67103","marks":["code"],"text":"signal"},{"id":"spn-67104","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67105","marks":["code"],"text":"digital"},{"id":"spn-67106","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67107","marks":["code"],"text":"mobility"},{"id":"spn-67108","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67109","marks":["code"],"text":"electrical"},{"id":"spn-67110","text":". A profile "},{"id":"spn-67111","marks":["bold"],"text":"declares"},{"id":"spn-67112","text":" domains; it is not one. And §D8.8's own recovery table already fixed the value for the frozen route at "},{"id":"spn-67113","marks":["code"],"text":"domain = signal"},{"id":"spn-67114","text":" — so the adapter was contradicting a normative table sitting 300 lines away in the same document."}]},{"id":"blk-41356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67115","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repair."},{"id":"spn-67116","text":" A declared map, not an expression:"}]},{"id":"blk-41357","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"export const PROFILE_DEFAULT_DOMAIN = deepFreeze({ \"forge.world.core.v1\": \"signal\" });\nexport function profileDefaultDomain(profileId)   // → WRL_UNKNOWN_PROFILE_DOMAIN"},{"id":"blk-41358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67117","text":"An unknown profile is refused rather than defaulted, because defaulting is how the original defect would come back."}]},{"id":"blk-41359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67118","marks":["bold"],"text":"Consequence I did not expect, and want you to look at."},{"id":"spn-67119","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67120","marks":["code"],"text":"domain"},{"id":"spn-67121","text":" moved out of the "},{"id":"spn-67122","marks":["bold"],"text":"free"},{"id":"spn-67123","text":" row of the field partition and into "},{"id":"spn-67124","marks":["bold"],"text":"no V1 form"},{"id":"spn-67125","text":". It had been filed free on the reasoning \"a V1 edge writes no domain, so changing one cannot disturb the id\" — true, and irrelevant. A V1 edge writes no domain because it is "},{"id":"spn-67126","marks":["italic"],"text":"entirely"},{"id":"spn-67127","text":" a signal-domain encoding; its two kinds are the two kinds of that one domain. An "},{"id":"spn-67128","marks":["code"],"text":"electrical"},{"id":"spn-67129","text":" relation is therefore not a relation whose domain V1 forgets to mention, it is one V1 "},{"id":"spn-67130","marks":["bold"],"text":"cannot represent"},{"id":"spn-67131","text":" — exactly like an "},{"id":"spn-67132","marks":["code"],"text":"acausal"},{"id":"spn-67133","text":" one. So the projection now refuses it, and the partition reads:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-41361","spans":[{"id":"spn-67134","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-41362","spans":[{"id":"spn-67135","text":"fields"}]},{"id":"blk-41363","spans":[{"id":"spn-67136","text":""}]}],"id":"blk-41360","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-41364","spans":[{"id":"spn-67137","text":"names it"}]},{"id":"blk-41365","spans":[{"id":"spn-67138","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-67139","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67140","marks":["code"],"text":"endpoints"}]},{"id":"blk-41366","spans":[{"id":"spn-67141","text":"2"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41367","spans":[{"id":"spn-67142","text":"free"}]},{"id":"blk-41368","spans":[{"id":"spn-67143","marks":["code"],"text":"policy"}]},{"id":"blk-41369","spans":[{"id":"spn-67144","text":"1"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41370","spans":[{"id":"spn-67145","text":"no V1 form"}]},{"id":"blk-41371","spans":[{"id":"spn-67146","marks":["code"],"text":"domain"},{"id":"spn-67147","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67148","marks":["code"],"text":"orientation"},{"id":"spn-67149","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67150","marks":["code"],"text":"texture"},{"id":"spn-67151","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67152","marks":["code"],"text":"attributes"}]},{"id":"blk-41372","spans":[{"id":"spn-67153","text":"4"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-41373","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67154","text":"Four of seven, not three. The spec's numeric claim was updated to match."}]},{"id":"blk-41374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67155","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checks."},{"id":"spn-67156","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67157","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/only-the-key-names-the-relation"},{"id":"spn-67158","text":" (partition, mutating each field in turn and classifying the result), "},{"id":"spn-67159","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/revision-field-partition-is-total"},{"id":"spn-67160","text":" (the partition covers "},{"id":"spn-67161","marks":["code"],"text":"REVISION_FIELDS"},{"id":"spn-67162","text":" exactly), "},{"id":"spn-67163","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/the-import-supplies-only-declared-constants"},{"id":"spn-67164","text":" (asserts the resolved domain is "},{"id":"spn-67165","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-67166","text":" the profile id — the specific defect, named)."}]},{"id":"blk-41375","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67167","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-67168","marks":["code"],"text":"texture = solid"},{"id":"spn-67169","text":", and directed-texture enforcement"}]},{"id":"blk-41376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67170","text":"You rejected my decision #1 with \"V1 semantically implies "},{"id":"spn-67171","marks":["code"],"text":"solid"},{"id":"spn-67172","text":"; restore and enforce it.\" Implemented, and you were right for a reason I had not seen."}]},{"id":"blk-41377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67173","marks":["bold"],"text":"Was."},{"id":"spn-67174","text":" The adapter emitted no "},{"id":"spn-67175","marks":["code"],"text":"texture"},{"id":"spn-67176","text":" key. My argument: a missing key and a "},{"id":"spn-67177","marks":["code"],"text":"texture: null"},{"id":"spn-67178","text":" are different claims, and no V1 world ever "},{"id":"spn-67179","marks":["italic"],"text":"considered"},{"id":"spn-67180","text":" texture, so inventing one would put an authored-looking value in an artifact that never carried it."}]},{"id":"blk-41378","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67181","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is wrong."},{"id":"spn-67182","text":" That argument answers "},{"id":"spn-67183","marks":["italic"],"text":"may the adapter invent a value?"},{"id":"spn-67184","text":" when the question is "},{"id":"spn-67185","marks":["italic"],"text":"what does this encoding mean?"},{"id":"spn-67186","text":" §5 gives V1 exactly one writable texture, "},{"id":"spn-67187","marks":["code"],"text":"--"},{"id":"spn-67188","text":" solid. So a V1 structural edge does not "},{"id":"spn-67189","marks":["bold"],"text":"omit"},{"id":"spn-67190","text":" a texture, it "},{"id":"spn-67191","marks":["bold"],"text":"elides"},{"id":"spn-67192","text":" one — the same relationship the artifact has to "},{"id":"spn-67193","marks":["code"],"text":"orientation"},{"id":"spn-67194","text":", which the adapter had been restoring all along without anyone calling it authorship. The test is whether the omitted value is "},{"id":"spn-67195","marks":["italic"],"text":"determined"},{"id":"spn-67196","text":", not whether the bytes contain it."}]},{"id":"blk-41379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67197","marks":["bold"],"text":"What the mistake actually cost"},{"id":"spn-67198","text":", which is the part I think is worth keeping on the page: it made "},{"id":"spn-67199","marks":["italic"],"text":"texture required for directed"},{"id":"spn-67200","text":" — a rule §D8.7 "},{"id":"spn-67201","marks":["bold"],"text":"states"},{"id":"spn-67202","text":" — unenforceable, because the kernel's own relations violated it. So the rule got filed as a V2 obligation, and §D8's texture row shipped as one enforced half and one commented half. A table with a commented row has stopped being a table."}]},{"id":"blk-41380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67203","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repair."},{"id":"spn-67204","text":" Both halves now come off one declaration:"}]},{"id":"blk-41381","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"export const ORIENTATION_TEXTURE = deepFreeze({\n  directed: \"required\", symmetric: \"optional\", acausal: \"forbidden\",\n});\nexport const TEXTURES   = deepFreeze([\"solid\", \"async\", \"verified\", \"fault\"]);\nexport const V1_TEXTURE = \"solid\";"},{"id":"blk-41382","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67205","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_MISSING_TEXTURE"},{"id":"spn-67206","text":" is new. "},{"id":"spn-67207","marks":["code"],"text":"projectRelationRevisionToV1Edge"},{"id":"spn-67208","text":" now "},{"id":"spn-67209","marks":["italic"],"text":"elides"},{"id":"spn-67210","text":" a solid texture on the way out and refuses any other — where the 0.1.1 rule was the opposite, "},{"id":"spn-67211","marks":["italic"],"text":"refuse any texture"},{"id":"spn-67212","text":", which round-tripped only because the adapter had never restored one."}]},{"id":"blk-41383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67213","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checks."},{"id":"spn-67214","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67215","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/directed-carries-a-texture"},{"id":"spn-67216","text":" (missing → "},{"id":"spn-67217","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_MISSING_TEXTURE"},{"id":"spn-67218","text":", and the well-formed one still accepted — both halves, so a validator that refused everything would not pass), "},{"id":"spn-67219","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/acausal-carries-no-texture"},{"id":"spn-67220","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67221","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/texture-vocabulary-is-the-specs"},{"id":"spn-67222","text":" (asserts §5's "},{"id":"spn-67223","marks":["bold"],"text":"four"},{"id":"spn-67224","text":" and that V1 writes one of them; narrowing the model's enumeration to what the surface can write would delete three guarantee classes while every other texture check still passed)."}]},{"id":"blk-41384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67225","marks":["bold"],"text":"Test-authoring note."},{"id":"spn-67226","text":" Two acausal specimens were silently testing the wrong rule after this change: they spread a directed "},{"id":"spn-67227","marks":["code"],"text":"base"},{"id":"spn-67228","text":" that now carries "},{"id":"spn-67229","marks":["code"],"text":"solid"},{"id":"spn-67230","text":", so they failed on "},{"id":"spn-67231","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_ACAUSAL_TEXTURE"},{"id":"spn-67232","text":" under names like "},{"id":"spn-67233","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/canonical-order-is-role-then-terminal"},{"id":"spn-67234","text":". The specimen builder now drops an inherited texture for acausal unless the check is deliberately supplying one. And "},{"id":"spn-67235","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/acausal-carries-no-texture"},{"id":"spn-67236","text":" now supplies a "},{"id":"spn-67237","marks":["bold"],"text":"legal"},{"id":"spn-67238","text":" texture, because an invented one ("},{"id":"spn-67239","marks":["code"],"text":"\"braided\""},{"id":"spn-67240","text":") is refused by the vocabulary first and leaves the orientation rule untested. Same class of error as the \"a law about a seam must parse, not grep\" rule."}]},{"id":"blk-41385","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67241","text":"3. Semantic-ID / artifact binding"}]},{"id":"blk-41386","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67242","marks":["bold"],"text":"Was."},{"id":"spn-67243","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67244","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveRelations(artifact, semanticId)"},{"id":"spn-67245","text":" took the world id as an argument and trusted it. Callers passed the one "},{"id":"spn-67246","marks":["code"],"text":"sealWorld"},{"id":"spn-67247","text":" had just returned, so it was always right, and it was checked by nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-41387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67248","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is wrong."},{"id":"spn-67249","text":" You demonstrated it: an artifact handed over with "},{"id":"spn-67250","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-000…0"},{"id":"spn-67251","text":" beside it minted a complete, well-formed set of relation ids scoped to a world that does not exist. A world-scoped identity is only as scoped as the world id it is scoped "},{"id":"spn-67252","marks":["italic"],"text":"to"},{"id":"spn-67253","text":", and a value whose meaning depends on an unverified claim travelling next to it has no meaning. The failure is silent — every id well-formed, every round trip green."}]},{"id":"blk-41388","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67254","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repair."},{"id":"spn-67255","text":" The id is "},{"id":"spn-67256","marks":["bold"],"text":"recomputed"},{"id":"spn-67257","text":" from the artifact's own canonical bytes inside "},{"id":"spn-67258","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveRelations"},{"id":"spn-67259","text":"; a supplied "},{"id":"spn-67260","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-"},{"id":"spn-67261","text":" becomes a cross-check refused on mismatch ("},{"id":"spn-67262","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_SEMANTIC_ID_MISMATCH"},{"id":"spn-67263","text":"). The recomputed path is the "},{"id":"spn-67264","marks":["italic"],"text":"only"},{"id":"spn-67265","text":" path — there is no faster one to fall back to. "},{"id":"spn-67266","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveLegacyEdgeCorrespondence"},{"id":"spn-67267","text":" routes both of its sides through the same checked boundary, so a sealed-looking record carrying a forged id is refused there too rather than only in the single-world path."}]},{"id":"blk-41389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67268","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checks."},{"id":"spn-67269","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67270","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/a-forged-world-id-is-refused"},{"id":"spn-67271","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67272","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/the-world-id-is-recomputed-not-supplied"},{"id":"spn-67273","text":" (running with "},{"id":"spn-67274","marks":["bold"],"text":"no"},{"id":"spn-67275","text":" claim gives the same ids — so the two paths cannot disagree and there is no unchecked way in)."}]},{"id":"blk-41390","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67276","text":"4. Explicit V1 source-version validation"}]},{"id":"blk-41391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67277","text":"The adapter's constants — "},{"id":"spn-67278","marks":["code"],"text":"directed"},{"id":"spn-67279","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67280","marks":["code"],"text":"solid"},{"id":"spn-67281","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67282","marks":["code"],"text":"signal"},{"id":"spn-67283","text":", the frozen port pairs — are V1's elisions. Applied to an artifact of a later version whose elisions differ, they would not fail; they would produce confident, wrong relations."}]},{"id":"blk-41392","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"export const V1_IR_VERSIONS = deepFreeze([\"1.0\", \"1.1\"]);\nexport function assertV1Artifact(artifact)   // → WRL_UNSUPPORTED_IR_VERSION"},{"id":"blk-41393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67284","text":"Called before any edge is read, on both the single-world and the correspondence paths."}]},{"id":"blk-41394","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67285","marks":["bold"],"text":"Check."},{"id":"spn-67286","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67287","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/an-unknown-ir-version-is-refused"},{"id":"spn-67288","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67289","marks":["bold"],"text":"Flagged:"},{"id":"spn-67290","text":" I admitted "},{"id":"spn-67291","marks":["code"],"text":"\"1.1\""},{"id":"spn-67292","text":" alongside "},{"id":"spn-67293","marks":["code"],"text":"\"1.0\""},{"id":"spn-67294","text":" because the frozen corpus contains both and the elisions are identical across them. If you consider that too permissive — i.e. that the adapter should be pinned to exactly the versions whose elisions it has been "},{"id":"spn-67295","marks":["italic"],"text":"tested"},{"id":"spn-67296","text":" against — say so and I will narrow it."}]},{"id":"blk-41396","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67297","text":"5. Deep-frozen identity tables"}]},{"id":"blk-41397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67298","marks":["bold"],"text":"Was."},{"id":"spn-67299","text":" Every exported vocabulary was an ordinary array or object."}]},{"id":"blk-41398","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67300","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is wrong."},{"id":"spn-67301","text":" You reversed "},{"id":"spn-67302","marks":["code"],"text":"ENDPOINT_ROLES"},{"id":"spn-67303","text":" and widened "},{"id":"spn-67304","marks":["code"],"text":"ORIENTATION_ROLES"},{"id":"spn-67305","text":" after import, and canonicalisation obligingly produced a different id for the same relation and admitted roles §D8 forbids. The role enumeration is not merely a list — it is the "},{"id":"spn-67306","marks":["bold"],"text":"sort key"},{"id":"spn-67307","text":" of the canonical form. A closed enumeration a consumer can reopen is an open enumeration with a comment attached."}]},{"id":"blk-41399","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67308","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repair."},{"id":"spn-67309","text":" A recursive "},{"id":"spn-67310","marks":["code"],"text":"deepFreeze"},{"id":"spn-67311","text":" applied to every exported table: "},{"id":"spn-67312","marks":["code"],"text":"ENDPOINT_ROLES"},{"id":"spn-67313","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67314","marks":["code"],"text":"ORIENTATIONS"},{"id":"spn-67315","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67316","marks":["code"],"text":"TEXTURES"},{"id":"spn-67317","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67318","marks":["code"],"text":"ORIENTATION_ROLES"},{"id":"spn-67319","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67320","marks":["code"],"text":"ORIENTATION_TEXTURE"},{"id":"spn-67321","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67322","marks":["code"],"text":"ALLOCATION_FIELDS"},{"id":"spn-67323","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67324","marks":["code"],"text":"PROFILE_DEFAULT_DOMAIN"},{"id":"spn-67325","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67326","marks":["code"],"text":"V1_IR_VERSIONS"},{"id":"spn-67327","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67328","marks":["code"],"text":"RELATION_IMPORTED_FIELDS"},{"id":"spn-67329","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67330","marks":["code"],"text":"REVISION_FIELDS"},{"id":"spn-67331","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41400","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67332","marks":["bold"],"text":"Check."},{"id":"spn-67333","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67334","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/immutability/the-canon-cannot-be-moved-from-outside"},{"id":"spn-67335","text":" — tampers with all of them, then re-asserts canonical order "},{"id":"spn-67336","marks":["italic"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-67337","text":" role legality. It checks the consequence, not the "},{"id":"spn-67338","marks":["code"],"text":"Object.isFrozen"},{"id":"spn-67339","text":" flag."}]},{"id":"blk-41401","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67340","text":"6. Correspondence separated from "},{"id":"spn-67341","marks":["code"],"text":"RelationImported"}]},{"id":"blk-41402","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67342","text":"This is the item I think was most valuable, and I want to state the general rule rather than just the fix."}]},{"id":"blk-41403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67343","marks":["bold"],"text":"Was."},{"id":"spn-67344","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67345","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveCorrespondence"},{"id":"spn-67346","text":" returned a field called "},{"id":"spn-67347","marks":["code"],"text":"imported"},{"id":"spn-67348","text":", whose entries had the four fields of a "},{"id":"spn-67349","marks":["code"],"text":"RelationImported"},{"id":"spn-67350","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67351","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is wrong."},{"id":"spn-67352","text":" The arithmetic was fine. What was wrong is that a "},{"id":"spn-67353","marks":["italic"],"text":"derivation"},{"id":"spn-67354","text":" produced a record whose entire content is "},{"id":"spn-67355","marks":["italic"],"text":"an operation was accepted"},{"id":"spn-67356","text":" — from two artifacts, which know nothing about operations. Read strictly it says two worlds are related by a migration because they contain matching edge keys, so two unrelated worlds built from the same starter template would be full of imports nobody performed."}]},{"id":"blk-41405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67357","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repair."},{"id":"spn-67358","text":" Three functions where there was one:"}]},{"id":"blk-41406","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"deriveLegacyEdgeCorrespondence(from, to)  // structural, derived: { pairs, dropped, added }\ncandidateImportedFacts(correspondence)    // what a fact would have to be backed by\ncheckRelationImported(facts, corr)        // the join → WRL_UNVERIFIED_IMPORT"},{"id":"blk-41407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67359","marks":["bold"],"text":"The rule underneath it."},{"id":"spn-67360","text":" Derived values do not need checking against their own inputs; "},{"id":"spn-67361","marks":["bold"],"text":"asserted"},{"id":"spn-67362","text":" ones do. "},{"id":"spn-67363","marks":["code"],"text":"RelationImported"},{"id":"spn-67364","text":" is emitted by an accepted migration operation, which makes it — uniquely in this kernel — a thing that can be "},{"id":"spn-67365","marks":["italic"],"text":"maintained wrongly"},{"id":"spn-67366","text":", which is exactly why it is the one thing joined against something derived. Merging the two loses the only join that could catch a wrong assertion, and loses it by making the assertion "},{"id":"spn-67367","marks":["bold"],"text":"unfalsifiable"},{"id":"spn-67368","text":" rather than by making it false."}]},{"id":"blk-41408","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67369","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checks."},{"id":"spn-67370","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67371","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/a-pairing-is-not-an-import-fact"},{"id":"spn-67372","text":" (asserts "},{"id":"spn-67373","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveCorrespondence"},{"id":"spn-67374","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-67375","marks":["italic"],"text":"gone"},{"id":"spn-67376","text":", that no "},{"id":"spn-67377","marks":["code"],"text":"imported"},{"id":"spn-67378","text":" key exists, and that a pair entry's keys are exactly "},{"id":"spn-67379","marks":["code"],"text":"key"},{"id":"spn-67380","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-67381","marks":["code"],"text":"from_relation"},{"id":"spn-67382","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-67383","marks":["code"],"text":"to_relation"},{"id":"spn-67384","text":"), "},{"id":"spn-67385","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/an-unbacked-import-fact-is-refused"},{"id":"spn-67386","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67387","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/the-fact-has-exactly-four-fields"},{"id":"spn-67388","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67389","marks":["code"],"text":"playground.html"},{"id":"spn-67390","text":" was updated to the new API and re-verified live — it renders "},{"id":"spn-67391","marks":["code"],"text":"3 paired · 1 dropped · 0 added"},{"id":"spn-67392","text":" against the pinned fixture."}]},{"id":"blk-41410","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67393","text":"7. Empty-world correspondence"}]},{"id":"blk-41411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67394","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/an-empty-world-still-corresponds-to-itself"},{"id":"spn-67395","text":" — a world with no relations mapped against itself reports "},{"id":"spn-67396","marks":["code"],"text":"identityPreserved: true"},{"id":"spn-67397","text":" with all three lists empty. This is the degenerate case a correspondence that fails by returning nothing would be "},{"id":"spn-67398","marks":["bold"],"text":"indistinguishable"},{"id":"spn-67399","text":" from, which is why you asked for it and why the other migration checks do not cover it. Verified live in the playground on the \"Empty world\" preset as well."}]},{"id":"blk-41412","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67400","text":"8. The missing model-register rows, and the B7 re-stage"}]},{"id":"blk-41413","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67401","text":"The register went "},{"id":"spn-67402","marks":["bold"],"text":"34 → 47 rows"},{"id":"spn-67403","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-67404","marks":["code"],"text":"model · executable"},{"id":"spn-67405","text":" went "},{"id":"spn-67406","marks":["bold"],"text":"22 → 35"},{"id":"spn-67407","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-67408","marks":["code"],"text":"model · awaiting"},{"id":"spn-67409","text":" remains "},{"id":"spn-67410","marks":["bold"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-67411","text":", so the "},{"id":"spn-67412","marks":["code"],"text":"REGISTERED_MODEL_DEBT_CAP = 0"},{"id":"spn-67413","text":" ratchet holds."}]},{"id":"blk-41414","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67414","text":"8a. The B7 split you ordered"}]},{"id":"blk-41415","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67415","text":"Two rows were "},{"id":"spn-67416","marks":["italic"],"text":"half"},{"id":"spn-67417","text":" misfiled, and I think this is the sharpest instance of the register's own failure mode that has come up:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-41417","spans":[{"id":"spn-67418","text":"law"}]},{"id":"blk-41418","spans":[{"id":"spn-67419","text":"was"}]},{"id":"blk-41419","spans":[{"id":"spn-67420","text":"is now"}]}],"id":"blk-41416","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-41420","spans":[{"id":"spn-67421","marks":["code"],"text":"same-name-different-world-differs"}]},{"id":"blk-41421","spans":[{"id":"spn-67422","text":"surface · awaiting"}]},{"id":"blk-41422","spans":[{"id":"spn-67423","marks":["bold"],"text":"split"},{"id":"spn-67424","text":": "},{"id":"spn-67425","marks":["code"],"text":"named-allocation-is-world-scoped"},{"id":"spn-67426","text":" (model · executable) + itself, narrowed, still surface · awaiting"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41423","spans":[{"id":"spn-67427","marks":["code"],"text":"overlapping-grants-do-not-collide"}]},{"id":"blk-41424","spans":[{"id":"spn-67428","text":"runtime · awaiting"}]},{"id":"blk-41425","spans":[{"id":"spn-67429","marks":["bold"],"text":"split"},{"id":"spn-67430","text":": "},{"id":"spn-67431","marks":["code"],"text":"granted-allocation-separates-grants"},{"id":"spn-67432","text":" (model · executable) + itself, narrowed, still runtime · awaiting"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-41426","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67433","text":"Both were filed correctly "},{"id":"spn-67434","marks":["italic"],"text":"as far as it went"},{"id":"spn-67435","text":" — there is no syntax for naming a relation and no machinery for issuing a grant. But an identity is a function of a "},{"id":"spn-67436","marks":["bold"],"text":"preimage"},{"id":"spn-67437","text":", and both preimages are writable today: a "},{"id":"spn-67438","marks":["code"],"text":"NamedInitialAllocation"},{"id":"spn-67439","text":" carries its "},{"id":"spn-67440","marks":["code"],"text":"world_id"},{"id":"spn-67441","text":", a "},{"id":"spn-67442","marks":["code"],"text":"GrantedAllocation"},{"id":"spn-67443","text":" carries its "},{"id":"spn-67444","marks":["code"],"text":"grant_id"},{"id":"spn-67445","text":". The arithmetic was never blocked; only the way a "},{"id":"spn-67446","marks":["italic"],"text":"person"},{"id":"spn-67447","text":" reaches it was. A single row covering both had the effect of hiding a settled property behind an unsettled one, and reported "},{"id":"spn-67448","marks":["bold"],"text":"less"},{"id":"spn-67449","text":" than was known."}]},{"id":"blk-41427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67450","text":"This is what forced the three-authorities separation:"}]},{"id":"blk-41428","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67451","marks":["bold"],"text":"Which variants exist"},{"id":"spn-67452","text":" — all three. "},{"id":"spn-67453","marks":["code"],"text":"relationIdFromAllocation"},{"id":"spn-67454","text":" mints any"}]}],"id":"blk-41429","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-41431","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67455","text":"well-formed allocation, and mints it the same way for everyone."}]},{"id":"blk-41432","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41434","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67456","marks":["bold"],"text":"Which a trusted importer may construct"},{"id":"spn-67457","text":" — only "},{"id":"spn-67458","marks":["code"],"text":"legacy-edge"},{"id":"spn-67459","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-41433","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41436","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67460","marks":["bold"],"text":"Which an authoring surface may emit"},{"id":"spn-67461","text":" — none, today."}]}],"id":"blk-41435","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-41437","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67462","marks":["code"],"text":"assertImportableAllocation"},{"id":"spn-67463","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-67464","marks":["code"],"text":"assertAuthorableAllocation"},{"id":"spn-67465","text":" are separate boundaries; the mint refuses nothing. Folding them into the hash, as 0.1.1 did, made identity depend on "},{"id":"spn-67466","marks":["bold"],"text":"who was asking"},{"id":"spn-67467","text":" — which is the property a content address exists to not have."}]},{"id":"blk-41438","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67468","text":"8b. The other new rows"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-41440","spans":[{"id":"spn-67469","text":"law"}]},{"id":"blk-41441","spans":[{"id":"spn-67470","text":"check"}]}],"id":"blk-41439","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-41442","spans":[{"id":"spn-67471","marks":["code"],"text":"directed-carries-a-texture"}]},{"id":"blk-41443","spans":[{"id":"spn-67472","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/directed-carries-a-texture"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41444","spans":[{"id":"spn-67473","marks":["code"],"text":"texture-vocabulary-is-closed"}]},{"id":"blk-41445","spans":[{"id":"spn-67474","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/texture-vocabulary-is-the-specs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41446","spans":[{"id":"spn-67475","marks":["code"],"text":"declared-vocabularies-are-immutable"}]},{"id":"blk-41447","spans":[{"id":"spn-67476","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/immutability/the-canon-cannot-be-moved-from-outside"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41448","spans":[{"id":"spn-67477","marks":["code"],"text":"allocation-variants-have-declared-fields"}]},{"id":"blk-41449","spans":[{"id":"spn-67478","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/allocations/each-variant-has-exactly-its-declared-fields"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41450","spans":[{"id":"spn-67479","marks":["code"],"text":"relation-id-binds-to-the-artifact-it-claims"}]},{"id":"blk-41451","spans":[{"id":"spn-67480","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/a-forged-world-id-is-refused"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41452","spans":[{"id":"spn-67481","marks":["code"],"text":"world-id-is-recomputed-not-supplied"}]},{"id":"blk-41453","spans":[{"id":"spn-67482","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/the-world-id-is-recomputed-not-supplied"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41454","spans":[{"id":"spn-67483","marks":["code"],"text":"import-admits-only-declared-artifact-versions"}]},{"id":"blk-41455","spans":[{"id":"spn-67484","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/binding/an-unknown-ir-version-is-refused"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41456","spans":[{"id":"spn-67485","marks":["code"],"text":"an-empty-world-corresponds-to-itself"}]},{"id":"blk-41457","spans":[{"id":"spn-67486","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/an-empty-world-still-corresponds-to-itself"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41458","spans":[{"id":"spn-67487","marks":["code"],"text":"a-pairing-is-not-an-import-fact"}]},{"id":"blk-41459","spans":[{"id":"spn-67488","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/a-pairing-is-not-an-import-fact"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41460","spans":[{"id":"spn-67489","marks":["code"],"text":"an-import-fact-is-backed-by-a-pairing"}]},{"id":"blk-41461","spans":[{"id":"spn-67490","marks":["code"],"text":"relation/migration/an-unbacked-import-fact-is-refused"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-41462","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67491","text":"Four existing rows had their "},{"id":"spn-67492","marks":["bold"],"text":"wording"},{"id":"spn-67493","text":" corrected rather than their status, because they were describing behaviour this commit changed: "},{"id":"spn-67494","marks":["code"],"text":"revision-does-not-move-relation-id"},{"id":"spn-67495","text":" (partition is now 2/1/4), "},{"id":"spn-67496","marks":["code"],"text":"import-supplies-only-declared-constants"},{"id":"spn-67497","text":" (adds the "},{"id":"spn-67498","marks":["italic"],"text":"resolved"},{"id":"spn-67499","text":" class; texture is no longer \"a missing key, never a null\"), "},{"id":"spn-67500","marks":["code"],"text":"import-mints-one-allocation-variant"},{"id":"spn-67501","text":" (the refusal moved from the mint to the two writer boundaries), "},{"id":"spn-67502","marks":["code"],"text":"migration-correspondence-is-derivable"},{"id":"spn-67503","text":" (no longer calls the derived pairing a "},{"id":"spn-67504","marks":["code"],"text":"RelationImported"},{"id":"spn-67505","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-41463","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67506","text":"9. What I need from you"}]},{"id":"blk-41464","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67507","text":"9a. Two decisions I took autonomously"}]},{"id":"blk-41465","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41467","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67508","marks":["bold"],"text":"`V1_IR_VERSIONS = [\"1.0\", \"1.1\"]`"},{"id":"spn-67509","text":" — see §4. Narrow it if you disagree."}]}],"id":"blk-41466","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41469","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67510","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-67511","marks":["code"],"text":"ir_version"},{"id":"spn-67512","text":" and profile are checked; the "},{"id":"spn-67513","marks":["italic"],"text":"rulepack"},{"id":"spn-67514","text":" is not.** The adapter"}]}],"id":"blk-41468","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-41470","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67515","text":"reads "},{"id":"spn-67516","marks":["code"],"text":"semantic_policies.rulepack_id"},{"id":"spn-67517","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-67518","marks":["code"],"text":"policy"},{"id":"spn-67519","text":" without validating it against a declared set, on the grounds that "},{"id":"spn-67520","marks":["code"],"text":"policy"},{"id":"spn-67521","text":" is the one "},{"id":"spn-67522","marks":["bold"],"text":"free"},{"id":"spn-67523","text":" field and so cannot reach an id. That is true today and stops being true the moment anything else consumes it. I left it, and I am flagging it rather than quietly relying on it."}]},{"id":"blk-41471","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67524","text":"9b. Path B — "},{"id":"spn-67525","marks":["bold"],"text":"answered, and built"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41473","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67526","text":"The two questions below were the ones I could not answer myself. You ruled both, and Path B is now built to that ruling: "},{"id":"spn-67527","marks":["code"],"text":"relations"},{"id":"spn-67528","text":" replaces "},{"id":"spn-67529","marks":["code"],"text":"edges"},{"id":"spn-67530","text":" outright at V2, §D8.8's projection is the V1 compatibility adapter only, and "},{"id":"spn-67531","marks":["code"],"text":"NamedInitialAllocation"},{"id":"spn-67532","text":"'s surface landed "},{"id":"spn-67533","marks":["italic"],"text":"inside"},{"id":"spn-67534","text":" B as slice B.4. Slices B.1 – B.5 are green at 828/828 with model debt 0. "},{"id":"spn-67535","marks":["bold"],"text":"See `HANDOFF_D8_PATH_B.md`"},{"id":"spn-67536","text":" — this section is left standing as the record of where Path A stopped."}]}],"id":"blk-41472","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-41474","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67537","text":"I have your B1–B7 rulings. Path A is now closed on my side and I can start B under the byte-layout rulings, but B is a Semantic IR "},{"id":"spn-67538","marks":["bold"],"text":"V2"},{"id":"spn-67539","text":" design task, and the two things I do not have are:"}]},{"id":"blk-41475","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41477","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67540","text":"the V2 byte layout ruled at the level of detail A had — specifically: does the"}]}],"id":"blk-41476","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41478","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67541","marks":["code"],"text":"relations"},{"id":"spn-67542","text":" array replace "},{"id":"spn-67543","marks":["code"],"text":"edges"},{"id":"spn-67544","text":" outright at V2 or coexist with it, and does the frozen legacy projection of §D8.8 remain "},{"id":"spn-67545","marks":["bold"],"text":"normative"},{"id":"spn-67546","text":" at V2 or become a read-only import path?"}]},{"id":"blk-41479","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41481","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67547","text":"whether the surface for "},{"id":"spn-67548","marks":["code"],"text":"NamedInitialAllocation"},{"id":"spn-67549","text":" lands "},{"id":"spn-67550","marks":["italic"],"text":"inside"},{"id":"spn-67551","text":" B or after it."}]}],"id":"blk-41480","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41482","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67552","text":"B7's split leaves one "},{"id":"spn-67553","marks":["code"],"text":"surface · awaiting"},{"id":"spn-67554","text":" row that only a surface can close, and I would rather not invent naming syntax to close a register row."}]},{"id":"blk-41483","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67555","text":"Everything in this memo is committed as one A.3 closure commit inside "},{"id":"spn-67556","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL/"},{"id":"spn-67557","text":" (own repo "},{"id":"spn-67558","marks":["code"],"text":"c-u-l8er/WRL"},{"id":"spn-67559","text":", branch "},{"id":"spn-67560","marks":["code"],"text":"main"},{"id":"spn-67561","text":") — per your ruling, \"after that battery is green and the pinned V1 IDs remain unchanged\"."}]},{"id":"blk-41484","kind